# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit a filled-in copy.

# --- Map tiles -------------------------------------------------------------
# MapTiler vector tiles. Free key at https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/
# Required. With no key the map draws a plain ground colour and says "Basemap
# unavailable". There is deliberately no substitute provider: a silent swap
# makes a total rendering failure look like a dark style choice.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY=

# MapTiler style id used for the dark theme, when the key above is set.
# Defaults to "basic-v2-dark" if unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_STYLE=

# MapTiler style id used for the light theme. Defaults to "basic-v2".
# The basemap follows the UI theme, so both need to be set together.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_STYLE_LIGHT=

# --- Meeting source --------------------------------------------------------
# Which adapter serves the map. Unset (the default) reads the committed
# snapshot at data/meetings-snapshot.json — the production path, refreshed by
# `pnpm ingest composite` on a schedule. Set to `composite` for local
# development against the live vendor portals (never in production: a fetch
# per visitor against a public body's portal is the service degradation
# CLAUDE.md forbids, and five portals in sequence outlive a serverless
# timeout). Tests pin `mock` themselves.
WTP_MEETING_SOURCE=

# --- Ingestion -------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact address sent in the User-Agent by every source adapter that touches
# the network, so an administrator who sees our traffic in a log has somewhere
# to write. Identified traffic gets a conversation; anonymous traffic gets
# blocked.
#
# Optional. Unset, the User-Agent still names the project and links the repo —
# it just gives whoever wants to complain a slower route. Not committed with a
# value, because a personal address in a public repo is a separate decision.
INGEST_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# --- Officeholder and funding sources --------------------------------------
# NONE of these take a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. That prefix inlines the value into
# the client bundle and publishes it. All three are read server-side, inside an
# adapter, at build time.

# Congress.gov. Free key at https://api.congress.gov/sign-up/
# NOT needed for the officeholder roster — that is built from the public-domain
# unitedstates/congress-legislators bulk file, which needs no key at all. This
# is for the member `depiction` endpoint that supplies portraits and their
# attribution (tracker D20), and later for roll calls.
CONGRESS_API_KEY=

# Plural Open (ex-Open States), for state legislators.
# Free key at https://open.pluralpolicy.com — note that account is SEPARATE
# from a pluralpolicy.com account. Build against v3; the v2 GraphQL API is
# sunset. The key is passed as an `apikey` query parameter. Data is CC-0.
#
# NOT needed for the officeholder roster, which is built from the nightly CC-0
# bulk CSVs at data.openstates.org — no key, no login, three requests for three
# states. This key is for the GraphQL API, which nothing currently uses.
#
# The default tier is 500 GraphQL requests/day at 1 request/second. That is the
# reason for the bulk route rather than a preference: AZ, NJ and NH are ~620
# legislators, and a per-district fetch pattern would spend most of a day's
# quota in a single build. If GraphQL is ever used, serialize at 1 req/sec,
# cache hard, and print the request count so the ceiling is visible rather than
# discovered by hitting it.
PLURAL_API_KEY=

# OpenFEC. Free key at https://api.open.fec.gov/developers/
# DO NOT WIRE THIS YET. It belongs to the FUNDING evidence tier, and federal law
# restricts commercial use of contributor information (52 U.S.C. 30111(a)(4)) —
# tracker D14 has to record that finding before an adapter ships. Holding the
# key is not clearance to use it.
FEC_API_KEY=

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon Postgres connection string, from the Neon console.
# postgresql://user:password@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
# Unset in development: nothing on the map entry screen reads the database yet.
DATABASE_URL=
